# Sizing for the local overlay, in one place. up.sh, e2e/up.sh and the tests read
# this file; kustomization.yaml (and vault.yaml, mock-mcp/mock-mcp.yaml) carry
# the matching per-pod requests and limits, and tests/deploy/local-sizing.test.ts
# fails when the two disagree.
#
# PROVISIONAL: the floor below is a starting point, to be measured. It is
# "whatever passes verify-turns.sh twice in a row without a 'could not measure'
# on that host", and that run has not been done at this size yet. The only
# measurement so far is of the smaller topology (two gateways, two nodes,
# Postgres, Redis): a 3 CPU / 3.5 GB minikube node inside a 4 CPU / 6 GB Docker
# VM, which had roughly 100 MB free under verification load. The full topology
# adds a `finance` node, the dev Vault and the mock MCP server, so the node and
# the floor grew by the same margin (about 2.6 GB of VM beyond the node).

# Default size of the minikube node (overridable: SLAUDE_LOCAL_CPUS, SLAUDE_LOCAL_MEMORY).
LOCAL_NODE_CPUS=4
LOCAL_NODE_MEMORY_MB=4864

# Provisional minimum Docker VM that hosts that node. up.sh warns below it.
LOCAL_VM_FLOOR_CPUS=5
LOCAL_VM_FLOOR_MEMORY_MB=7680

# What the node keeps for itself (kubelet, apiserver, coredns, metrics-server).
# The summed pod LIMITS at the pinned replica counts must fit the node size
# minus these.
LOCAL_SYSTEM_RESERVE_MILLICPU=200
LOCAL_SYSTEM_RESERVE_MEMORY_MB=500

# Per-node-pod headroom. A node pod holds the bun process plus one `claude` CLI
# child per warm session, measured at roughly 150-200 MB each (the 2026-10-01
# remote-exec field note). The node limit must cover bun plus three warm
# sessions: 200 + 3 x 200 = 800 MB, so the 896 Mi limit leaves a little over.
LOCAL_NODE_BASE_MB=200
LOCAL_NODE_SESSION_MB=200
LOCAL_NODE_WARM_SESSIONS=3

# Limits arithmetic at the pinned counts (2 gateways, 2 default nodes, 1 finance
# node, Postgres, Redis, Vault, mock MCP):
#   memory: gateway 2 x 448 + node 3 x 896 + postgres 240 + redis 64
#           + vault 192 + mock-mcp 192 = 4272 MB; available 4864 - 500 = 4364 MB
#   cpu:    gateway 2 x 400 + node 3 x 700 + postgres 400 + redis 200
#           + vault 200 + mock-mcp 100 = 3800m; available 4000 - 200 = 3800m
# The documented flow can also deploy Keycloak (panel.sh: request 512 Mi, limit
# 1 Gi). It is NOT in the limits sum: limits are overcommitted by design for
# that optional add-on, and it is its REQUEST that must fit (with every pod at
# the HPA maximum of three default nodes). local-sizing.test.ts checks both.
